NOTES = [
    "Range: v7 299 frac ≈0.85 («والذي يُصَبُّ عليه الماء…», mid-line 5 of the 5 matn lines on 299) to v7 307 end («…تخريج غيرها من المسائل»). The previous file's card 10 ends at 299 frac 0.8 (same matn-line convention), so no overlap; the brief's '≈0.1–0.2' fraction would only fit a whole-page measure (most of 299 is footnotes), not the matn. Teacher's page refs (his copy): 1835 (0:05:55), 1839 (0:31:29). Next lesson (2025-10-05) starts كتاب الصيد (0:38:59).",
    "OCR v7 306 (PDF 307): contrary to the brief, the local file /home/claude/wifaq/v7ocr/p0306-0310.md DOES have a [متن] for printed 306 («ثم طبخ بماءه: إن كان الماء أسرع ذهاباً…» to «ولو قطع عنه النار»), and it joins cleanly with 305 («إذا صُبَّ عليه ماء قبل الطبخ،») and 307 («فغلي حتى ذهب الثلثان»). Card 8 therefore cites K7(306) for the second أصل. The file header warns '⚠ expected 5 pages, got 3' (PDF 309–310 are كتاب الصيد). OCR «بماءه» probably = «بمائه»; «لرقيقته» = «لرقته».",
    "Recording begins mid-sentence (0:00:00 «لیکن اس پر،»); 0:00:00–0:03:00 is the recap of the previous lesson, carded only as card 1 faida. In it (0:01:37–0:01:41) the teacher says flatly the three drinks are «نجاست خفیفہ» — the matn (v7 292) has two riwayat (خفيفة/غليظة); that line is not carded. «احناف کی راجح رائے» / «فتویٰ امام محمد پر» (0:00:16, 0:02:45, 0:38:32–0:38:47) and 'other fuqaha: hadd for a sip' (0:36:55–0:37:09) are not in the matn/footnotes; U-only, labelled «استاد».",
    "Card 1: teacher 0:05:12–0:05:30 says even if water and juice evaporate at the same rate 'the remainder is not one third of the grape juice, it may be more' — this contradicts الكفاية ٩/٣٨ (if they certainly went together it would be halal like the muthallath; haram only because water may go first) and the book's own second أصل (v7 306: together → boil the whole until 2/3 gone, halal), which the teacher himself explains correctly at 0:30:01–0:30:41. Card follows الكفاية/matn; 0:05:12–0:05:30 are not tagged. He also calls the juice «شراب» (0:04:11) in the example.",
    "Card 3: teacher 0:08:05 «اگر پکے ہوئے پانی کے اندر کھجور ڈال دیا جائے تو وہ ان کے ہاں حلال ہے» — not the book's case (cooked nabidh al-tamr is halal for the shaykhayn), and it clashes with the matn v7 301 (dates soaked in cooked naqi' in an amount from which nabidh is made → not halal). Not tagged. His «کھجور کے ملے ہوئے پانی» (0:07:32–0:07:39) is closer to the matn's second form «بين عصير العنب ونقيع التمر»; card mentions both.",
    "Card 4: teacher calls the «يملأ ماء مرة بعد أخرى» method 'Abu Yusuf's second قول' (0:14:17); matn «وقيل: عند أبي يوسف» — card labels it «کتاب: وقيل». The two reasons for the original prohibition and the two reasons for the later permission (0:11:54–0:12:31) are the teacher's; labelled «استاد». His hantam = clay matka matches زاذان's «الجرة» (البناية ١١/٤٥٢); البناية ١١/٤٥٠ says جرار حمر/خضر. The footnote quoting ابن عمر has «المزفت وهو النقير» (OCR/print oddity); not used.",
    "Card 5: teacher maps Shafi'i's two views onto 'خود بخود سرکہ بنی' (0:15:56–0:16:05). The matn says «بغير إلقاء شيء فيه»; البناية ١١/٤٥٥: that means treatment such as moving to the sun or lighting a fire nearby, and if it turns to vinegar by itself over time it is halal for them without dispute. Card gives the book's scope and notes the teacher's wording. Teacher says Shafi'i 'not jaiz' (0:15:45); matn «يكره التخليل». '20 litres… you can sell it' (0:17:50–0:17:52) is his example.",
    "Card 6: teacher calls dardi «جائز نہیں» / «حرام» (0:20:09, 0:21:56); matn «يكره». The matn's «لا يجوز أن يداوي به… ولا أن يسقي ذمياً…» follows «والانتفاع بالمحرّم حرام» (about khamr/dardi); «وكذا لا يسقيها الدواب» refers to khamr; teacher applies all to dardi — card keeps the matn wording. The «وقيل» (only carrying khamr to animals is barred; leading the animal to it is fine) is a single «قيل»; the teacher presents both as two views (0:20:39–0:20:57), consistent.",
    "Card 7: teacher defines الاحتقان as introducing medicine via the rear (0:23:59), and he mentions both front and rear at 0:23:52–0:23:54; matn pairs احتقان with إقطار في الإحليل (البناية: ثقب الذكر). He says «حرام/ناجائز» (0:24:07, 0:25:11); matn «يكره» — he himself explains مكروه = حرام here (0:25:11–0:25:35, teacher's general framing, carded as faida).",
    "Card 9: teacher's arithmetic slips: 333×600 given as «2000» (0:34:28) and «20,000» (0:34:56, 0:36:08) — it is ≈200,000 (book: 3⅓×6 = 20 in ratl units); at 0:36:13 he says «ضرب دیں گے» where he means divide; at 0:36:23 he gets «220» then says 222 (0:36:34). These timestamps are not tagged; card gives 333×600÷900 ≈ 222 (0:35:04–0:35:14). He calls this the «تیسرا اصول» (0:31:04, 0:31:27); the book introduces both the water rule and this one with «وأصل آخر». His first example (0:32:23–0:32:51: 1000→900, pour 100→800) is abandoned unfinished; not carded.",
    "Card 8: teacher's 850-ml example (0:27:22–0:27:50) works (300 is a third of 900, not of 850) but is confusing; the card uses his clean 1000→900→300 example (0:28:15–0:28:31). Interlinear glosses on 305–306 are empty ('—') except «العصير»; GLOSS cited only where a gloss exists.",
    "Footnote citations converted page-first → vol/page as in earlier files: الكفاية ٣٨/٩→٩/٣٨, ٣٩/٩, ٤٠/٩, ٤٠/٩-٤١→٩/٤٠–٤١, ٤١/٩; العناية ٣٩/٩, ٤٠/٩; البناية ٤٤٧/١١ … ٤٦٦/١١ → ١١/…; نصب الراية ٣٠٩/٤→٤/٣٠٩; نتائج الأفكار ٣٩/٩→٩/٣٩. Odd ones cited by name only: «[العناية ٣٧/١١]» (v7 299, the يوسفي/يعقوبي note; العناية is vol 9), «[نصب الراية ٤ / ٣١]» (v7 303, page looks truncated), «[نتائج الأفكار ٤٠٤١/٩]» (v7 305, merged digits; not used). Bare «(البناية)/(الكفاية)» cited by name. The مسلم takhrij for «نعم الإدام الخل» cited as «حاشیہ ص ٣٠٣».",
]
